DISCOVERY DEMAND B — CHILD PSYCHOLOGICAL EVALUATION

CASE: 1FDV-23-0001009
TO: Scot Stuart Brower, Esq. (Mother's Counsel)

DEFENDANT DEMANDS complete production of:

1. Any psychological evaluation or assessment of the child conducted in this case
2. Identity of the evaluator (name, credentials, licensing)
3. Date, location, and methodology of evaluation
4. Full psychological report (including raw scores, observations, recommendations)
5. All supporting materials (questionnaires, tests, interview notes)
6. Evaluator's communications with parties or counsel
7. Billing records for psychological services

IF NO EVALUATION EXISTS: Mother must provide sworn certification that no child psychological evaluation has been conducted, ordered, or completed in this case.

RESPONSE DUE: 14 calendar days from service
FORMAT: Native electronic file format

STATUTORY BASIS: HRS §571-46(b)(8) requires consideration of the psychological adjustment of the child to home, school, and community. Absence of evaluation must be affirmatively certified under oath.
